Third-party code in src/port/arm
================================

This folder holds three files from Arm Optimized Routines and two from
Android's bionic, kept byte for byte as published, with the details below.

libterae's own files here are port_memcpy.S, port_memmove.S, port_memset.S,
port_memcmp.S and private/bionic_asm.h. They are under libterae's licence,
given at the top of each. The four port_*.S files only rename the upstream
symbols and include the files below, and only they are assembled.
private/bionic_asm.h is not bionic's file of that name, which this folder
does not contain: it is libterae's replacement for it, defining the few
macros that bionic's memmove.S and memcmp.S use.

asmdefs.h here is Arm Optimized Routines' header for 32-bit Arm. The
project's AArch64 header has the same name and is in src/port/aarch64.
Each folder keeps its own copy, and memcpy.S includes it with quotes, which
finds the one beside it.


